{"path":"io/c/perror","title":"std::perror","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::</span>perror","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/io/c/perror","section":"io","kind":"page","summary":"Prints a textual description of the error code currently stored in the system variable errno to stderr.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-header\">\n<td> <div>Defined in header <code><a href=\"/w/cpp/header/cstdio\">&lt;cstdio&gt;</a></code>\n </div></td>\n<td></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl\">\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\"> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">void</span> perror<span class=\"br0\">(</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw4\">char</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>s <span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n<td class=\"t-dcl-nopad\">  </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Prints a textual description of the error code currently stored in the system variable <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno\">errno</a></span> to <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/std_streams\">stderr</a></span>.\n</p><p>The description is formed by concatenating the following components:\n</p>\n<ul><li> the contents of the null-terminated byte string pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code>, followed by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">\": \"</span></span></code> (unless <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code> is a null pointer or the character pointed to by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">s</span></code> is the null character).\n</li><li> implementation-defined error message string describing the error code stored in <code>errno</code>, followed by <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span></span></code>. The error message string is identical to the result of <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strerror\"><span class=\"kw1169\">std::<span class=\"me2\">strerror</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>.\n</li></ul>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<table class=\"t-par-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-par\">\n<td> s\n</td>\n<td> -\n</td>\n<td> pointer to a null-terminated string with explanatory message\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cerrno&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cmath&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;cstdio&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"kw4\">double</span> not_a_number <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/numeric/math/log\"><span class=\"kw1332\">std::<span class=\"me2\">log</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"nu16\">1.0</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <span class=\"kw1\">if</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"kw2\">errno</span> <span class=\"sy1\">==</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno_macros\"><span class=\"kw814\">EDOM</span></a><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        std<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">perror</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"log(-1) failed\"</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/c/fprintf\"><span class=\"kw1862\">std::<span class=\"me2\">printf</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"st0\">\"%f<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span>, not_a_number<span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>log(-1) failed: Numerical argument out of domain\nnan</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/error/errno\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>errno</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td> macro which expands to POSIX-compatible thread-local error number variable<br><span class=\"t-mark\">(macro variable)</span></td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/byte/strerror\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>strerror</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a text version of a given error code <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td colspan=\"2\"> <div class=\"t-dsc-see\"><span><a href=\"/w/c/io/perror\">C documentation</a></span> for <span class=\"t-dsc-see-tt\"><span>perror</span></span></div>\n</td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"io","title":"Input/output library"},{"path":"io/c","title":"C-style file input/output"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::perror","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"1 declaration. Prints a textual description of the error code currently stored in the system variable errno to stderr."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"s"},{"label":"Return value","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"errno","note":"macro which expands to POSIX-compatible thread-local error number variable"},{"label":"strerror","note":"returns a text version of a given error code"}]}]},"standards":[],"wordCount":168,"codeBlockCount":2}
